\date{2026-04-13T02:07:19Z}
\tag{discrete}

\import{discrete-macros}

\taxon{Example}

\p{Solve for #{x}: ##{x + 22 \equiv_{19} 20x + 3} Subtracting #{x + 3} from both sides yields ##{19 \equiv_{19} 19x.} But since #{19 \equiv_{19} 0}, this reduces to ##{0 \equiv_{19} 0,} which is always true for any value of #{x}. Hence every integer is a solution for #{x}.}
